## 4. The User Journey Map

*This matrix maps the user experience directly to the backend and frontend requirements. Customize the phases below to match your workflow (e.g., Discovery, Setup, Integration, Maintenance).*

| Journey Phase | 1. Discovery & Entry | 2. Authentication & Setup | 3. Core Action / Execution | 4. Confirmation & Next Steps |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **User Goal** | Wants to find out if the tool solves their immediate problem. | Needs to create an account and authenticate securely. | Executes the primary value proposition (e.g., runs a report). | Confirms success and knows how to repeat the value. |
| **User Action** | Clicks on the dashboard link from an email or landing page. | Fills out OAuth or credentials form; activates MFA. | Inputs data parameters and clicks "Generate". | Views success modal, downloads report, or copies code block. |
| **Touchpoints / UI Elements** | Landing Page, Email CTA, Guest Dashboard. | Sign-Up Page, MFA Modal, Email Verification Webhook. | Configuration Workspace, Input Fields, Loading Spinners. | Success Banner, Download Button, Documentation Links. |
| **User Mindset & Friction** | "Is this worth my time?" Worried about information overload. | "I hate long forms." Annoyed by slow email verification delays. | "Did it work?" Anxious if processing takes longer than 3 seconds. | "Great, what's next?" Wants to share or automate this. |
| **Frontend Requirements (UX/UI)** | • Responsive grid view.<br>• Skeleton loaders during initial paint.<br>• Clear CTA button. | • Inline form validation.<br>• Password strength indicator.<br>• Social login integrations. | • Real-time input validation.<br>• Progress bar for long-running states.<br>• Accessible tooltips. | • Clear success state visualization.<br>• One-click clipboard copy for code/tokens.<br>• Persistent download link. |
| **Backend & System Actions** | • Fetch user access token routing.<br>• Initialize session cookies.<br>• Fire analytics page-view event. | • Validate password complexity hash.<br>• Trigger verification email queue.<br>• Provision database user record. | • Process payload via processing engine pipeline.<br>• Cache query results (Redis).<br>• Enforce rate-limiting checks. |   • Generate signed download URL (S3 bucket).<br>• Update state database to 'Completed'.<br>• Emit webhook notification. |
| **Analytics & Telemetry Logs** | `page_view_landing` | `auth_success`, `auth_failed_reason` | `process_initiated`, `process_latency_ms` | `journey_complete`, `download_triggered` |

