## 5. Engineering Objectives & Technical Specs

*This section translates the journey map directly into engineering objectives. Group tasks logically by stack layer.*

### 5.1 Frontend Engineering (UI/UX)
* [ ] **Objective FE-1:** Build the step-by-step wizard UI conforming to the attached Figma specs (`[Link to Figma]`).
* [ ] **Objective FE-2:** Implement client-side validation on all forms to minimize unnecessary round-trip API requests.
* [ ] **Objective FE-3:** Ensure full accessibility (WCAG 2.1 AA compliance) across all newly introduced interface blocks.

### 5.2 Backend Engineering & Architecture
* [ ] **Objective BE-1:** Expose standard REST endpoints: `POST /api/v1/journey/start` and `GET /api/v1/journey/status/{id}`.
* [ ] **Objective BE-2:** Optimize database queries for the core processing pipeline to keep API response times under `200ms` at P95.
* [ ] **Objective BE-3:** Integrate the 3rd-party authentication provider/service via secure webhooks.

### 5.3 Data, Telemetry & Analytics
* [ ] **Objective DT-1:** Implement structured logging (JSON) across all lifecycle hooks mapped in the journey table (Section 4).
* [ ] **Objective DT-2:** Set up Segment/Mixpanel event tracking for each stage transition to measure drop-offs accurately.

